>> B5: Briefly describe your implementation of the "wait" system call
>> and how it interacts with process termination.

Each parent keeps one `child_process` record per direct child. `process_wait()`
rejects unknown or already-waited children, blocks on the child's semaphore,
then returns its saved exit status and frees the record. On termination, a
child saves its status and signals the semaphore. If the parent exits first,
ownership is released and the child frees the record after it terminates.

